--- WHAT THIS RUN ACTUALLY GRADES (named wrong implementations killed) ---
    Gradeability is NOT "two captures differing only in a setting differ in some cell". That test is
    false in both directions: LB-DEC31 reports ZERO cells differing across the day-count setting and
    still kills a no-arm port by 6,015 minor units (finding T55-N1). An all-products-identical capture
    is therefore not evidence of non-gradeability.
    counterfactuals named by GRADED vectors: 0  (0 money kills, 0 structural kills)
    kills carried by REFUSED vectors: 0, credited to NOTHING (0 corroboration claims likewise)
    kills carried by HARNESS-ERROR vectors: 0, credited to NOTHING (0 corroboration claims likewise)
        An errored vector is the strongest case of "graded nothing": a refusal is at least a
        decision about the vector, an error is the absence of one. Before A2-27 these credited
        the count above, so a run with NO implementation registered — 0 cells compared — printed
        113 kills and no UNBACKED claim at all. Reachable, not hypothetical: it is the standing
        state of cmd/conformance/impl_hook.go until a port is registered (finding A2-22-F3).
        A refusal is not a pass and not a failure: it says no discriminating vector exists here, or
        the seam is blind to the behaviour. A vector that graded nothing kills nothing, so its named
        kills do not enter the count above and do not remove a capability from the UNBACKED list.
        Until A2-22 they did both, and a refusal therefore made this report QUIETER — the one case
        with LESS evidence going silent (finding A2-19 F3).
    The two are NEVER merged. A MONEY kill separates the oracle from a wrong implementation by a
    non-zero minor-unit margin. A STRUCTURAL kill separates it by a cell that carries no money at
    all — a due date, a period boundary, a row kind, the row order — and its margin is honestly 0.
    P-02's month-end re-anchor and P-03's row ordering are graded ONLY structurally: every money
    column is identical to the baseline and the port is still wrong. A store of nothing but
    structural kills grades no amount, and this line is how a reader can tell (finding D-4).
    no graded capability is backed by a parity vector yet
    UNBACKED in_graded_domain claims: monthend.reanchor, schedule.core

